# 2FA setup checklist (backend)

> Generated by `php artisan auth:setup` (the light-it auth package). It lists what the
> package could not do for you, because it never edits your files. Tick each box,
> then **delete this file**. How 2FA works:
> https://github.com/Light-it-labs/lightit-auth-laravel/blob/main/docs/google-2fa.md

- [ ] **Wire the challenge into `LoginAction`** (`src/Authentication/Domain/Actions/LoginAction.php`).
  Inject the challenge action through the constructor:

```php
{{gateConstructorSnippet}}
```

- [ ] Then call it right after `$request->session()->regenerate();`, before `return $user;`:

```php
{{gateCallSnippet}}
```

- [ ] **Make `User` support 2FA**: `\Lightit\Users\Domain\Models\User` must extend
  `\Lightit\Authentication\Domain\TwoFactorAuthenticatable` instead of
  `Illuminate\Foundation\Auth\User`. In `src/Users/Domain/Models/User.php`, replace
  `use Illuminate\Foundation\Auth\User as Authenticatable;` with
  `use Lightit\Authentication\Domain\TwoFactorAuthenticatable;` (kept in alphabetical order
  with the other `use` lines) and `extends Authenticatable` with `extends TwoFactorAuthenticatable`.
  The TOTP secret's `encrypted` cast is built in.
- [ ] **Run `php artisan migrate`** (adds the 2FA columns to `users`).
- [ ] **Pick the mode** in `.env`: `TWO_FACTOR_AUTHENTICATION_MANDATORY=true` (the default:
  every user sets 2FA up at login) or `false` (only users who already set it up are asked
  for a code).

Check it worked: log in with a user. With `true`, the response is `200` with
`token_type: setup_required`; with `false`, a user without 2FA comes straight in.

Running `auth:setup` with 2FA again warns you while `LoginAction` or `User` still
need their change.
